Z||000000||Voyd||10-31-1999||01:48 PM||||ive already posted a msg on here with my problem, but here it is again.<P>i am having idle trouble, when i am stopped at a traffic light and  in the Drive position, for more than 20 seconds, the engine cuts out. it doesnt cut out in Park.<P>ok, so i did the ECM trouble code check and 2 codes were returned to me.<P>Code 33: Manifold Air Pressure Sensor(replace Air Pressure sensor)<BR>Code 44: Lean Exhaust (replace Oxygen sensor)<P>now that i have found the source of my problem, are changing these 2 parts hard, and how much will it cost me? finally, will changing these 2 parts eliminate the problem, or is it possible the computer missed something?<P>thanks||||reg||5
Z||000001||AL||10-31-1999||04:51 PM||||ok the map sensor is the one next to your plenum, it's a little black boxs with two screws,very easy. now the oxy sensor is on the left side of the car, when you lift your deck up look at the pipe next to the drivers side, you will see a connector on the pipe with a thin wire, disconnect wire and then go at it with the best possible way you can think of. it's all easy just look at it and study it and start turning those wrenches. good luck, and yes it will effect your car if you don't change them, Al.  ||||reg||14
